  "worked_solution": "Since $A\\,(1,1)$ lies on ${f}^{-1},$ we have ${f}^{-1}(1)=1.$\nWe're also told that ${f}^{\u2032}(1)=-2.$\n\nThe formula for the derivative of the inverse function is\n\n$$\n({f}^{-1})^{\u2032}(x)=\\frac{1}{{f}^{\u2032}({f}^{-1}(x))}.\n$$\n\nEvaluating at $x=1,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}({f}^{-1})^{\u2032}(1) & =\\frac{1}{{f}^{\u2032}({f}^{-1}(1))} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{{f}^{\u2032}(1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{(-2)} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
